This failure matters because it reveals a discrepancy between the high-level rule description and the actual implementation. The rule states 'no relaxation' [6ab8417a77f3b613], but the code explicitly uses `.casefold()` for the value-in-span check. A proposer should next look for cases where this implicit case-insensitivity in the value-in-span check (which is distinct from the span-in-document check) creates a divergence from a strict reading of 'no relaxation'.

